        <p>
          Group decisions usually stall in one of two places: nobody wants to be the first to speak up, or whoever breaks the tie gets accused of playing favorites. When you are calling on quiet seventh-graders, assigning sprint demo slots on Zoom, or running a charity prize draw in front of donors, picking manually puts unwanted social pressure on the host.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <strong>spin the wheel generator</strong> shifts the call onto a visible, neutral mechanism. You paste your options, spin once, and everyone watches the wheel decelerate together to the exact same winning slice. Below, we walk through how browser Web Cryptography calculates each spin without bias, how built-in weights and winner elimination actually work in practice, and how to set up a reusable wheel in under two minutes.
        </p>

